Magnetic field due to a circular loop at the centre of the loop is $B_1=\frac{\mu_0}{4 \pi} \frac{2 \pi I_c}{R}$. Magnetic field due to a straight line at the centre of the loop is $B_2=\frac{\mu_0 2 I_e}{4 \pi H}Both these fields act in opposite direction hence total magnetic field at the $centre of the loop is

\begin{aligned}
& B=B_1-B_2=$\frac{\mu_0 2 \pi I_c}{4 \pi R}-\frac{\mu_0 2 I_e}{4 \pi H}$ \\
& B=0 $\text{ (given). }$ \\
& \therefore $\frac{\mu_0 2 \pi I_c}{4 \pi R}=\frac{\mu_0 2 I_e}{4 \pi H} \text{ or, }$ H=$\frac{I_e R}{\pi I_c}$ .
\end{aligned}

